---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="AI Design Automation Repo | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="How I built the AI-powered design system that replaced how a 30-person Microsoft team designs, prototypes, and ships work."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--blue">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="container container--narrow">

        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back">← Back</a>

        <span class="tag">AI Systems · Product · Microsoft</span>
        <h1>The repo that changed how our team designs</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I built an AI-powered design automation system from scratch. Within weeks it was the
          primary tool for a 30-person design and PM team. It is used for prototyping, daily design
          work, and every senior leadership demo.
        </p>

        <div class="outcomes-strip">
          <div class="outcome"><span class="outcome__num">30+</span><span class="outcome__label">designers and PMs using it</span></div>
          <div class="outcome"><span class="outcome__num">Day 1</span><span class="outcome__label">adoption from first release</span></div>
          <div class="outcome"><span class="outcome__num">100%</span><span class="outcome__label">of senior leadership demos built with it</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="container container--narrow">

      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>
        Our design team was spending significant time on repeatable, manual work: generating
        early-stage designs, creating prototypes for PM customer interviews, building materials
        for senior leadership reviews. None of it required creative judgment. All of it required
        design knowledge.
      </p>
      <p>
        The tools available didn't understand our design language, couldn't pull in real product
        context, and produced output that needed significant rework before it was usable. There
        was no system. Everyone was improvising individually.
      </p>

      <h2>My role</h2>
      <p>
        I built it. End to end. I own the repo, its architecture, its processes, and its roadmap.
        That includes UX spec building, engineering handoff, requirements gathering from PMs and
        engineers, deciding what gets built, and onboarding the people who contribute to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work directly with PMs and engineers to understand what they need, sometimes building
        out what they describe, sometimes pushing back and building what they actually need based
        on my judgment of the problem.
      </p>

      <h2>What I built</h2>
      <p>
        A repo of AI skills and agents that generates designs using our exact Microsoft Fabric
        design language. The system has MCPs and APIs wired in for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Customer research and feedback</li>
        <li>Imagery and visual assets</li>
        <li>PM specs and PRDs</li>
        <li>Customer feedback and voice-of-customer data</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The result automates significant portions of the design process: prototyping, spec
        generation, and early-stage design exploration. It also enforces our quality standards,
        including content guidelines and accessibility requirements. It doesn't produce generic
        output. It produces work that looks and reads like our team made it, because the system
        knows our design language.
      </p>

      <h2>The outcome</h2>
      <p>
        The entire design and PM team in our business group uses it. That's roughly 10 designers
        on my immediate team, another 10 on the wider design team, and 10 PMs across both groups.
        Adoption was immediate. There was no slow rollout, forcing, or incentive. People switched
        because it was better.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's now the primary tool my design manager uses. When senior leadership visits, every
        demo is built with it. PMs use it to generate quick prototypes to take into customer
        interviews. I'm continuing to iterate, and the current focus is improving the engineering
        handoff process so what we produce moves cleanly into development.
      </p>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <div class="nav-row">
        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="btn btn--ghost">← All projects</a>
        <a href={`${base}/work/hackathon`} class="btn">Next: Hackathon win →</a>
      </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: 0; }
  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .tag { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); display: inline-block; }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--size-xl);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .outcomes-strip {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .outcome { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); }
  .outcome__num {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--size-4xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .outcome__label { font-size: var(--size-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: none; }

  h2 { margin-top: var(--space-12); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .btn:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); color: #fff; }
  .btn--ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .btn--ghost:hover { background: var(--color-tag-bg); color: var(--color-accent-hover); }
  .nav-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-4); }
</style>
